---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import SvgDefs from "../components/SvgDefs.astro"
import ThemeToggle from "../components/ThemeToggle.astro"
import { loginUrl } from "../lib/config"

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "AboutPage",
    name: "About Threa",
    url: new URL("/about", Astro.site).href,
    mainEntity: {
      "@type": "Person",
      name: "Kristoffer Remback",
      sameAs: ["https://github.com/kristofferremback", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/kristofferremback/"],
    },
  },
]
---

<Layout
  title="About · Threa"
  description="Why Kristoffer Remback built Threa, an open-source workplace chat app that keeps decisions linked to their source conversations."
  schema={schema}
>
  <SvgDefs />

  <!-- ============================================================
       HERO — premise stated plainly. Two columns so the masthead
       doesn't hug the left margin: headline left, framing right.
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="frame">
    <div class="hero-shell">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="nav-row">
          <div class="brand">
            <svg><use href="#threa-mark" /></svg>
            <span class="wordmark">Threa</span>
          </div>
          <nav class="nav-links">
            <a href="/">Product</a>
            <a href="/developers">Developer</a>
            <a href="/about" aria-current="page">About</a>
          </nav>
          <a class="nav-login" href={loginUrl}>Log in</a>
          <ThemeToggle />
        </div>

        <div class="about-hero">
          <h1 class="h-display">
            I built Threa out of<br />
            <span class="accent">curiosity</span> and<br />
            frustration.
          </h1>
          <p class="lede">
            My day job is software engineering, where I spend a lot of time in
            tools that are <em>fine</em>. Their small frustrations add up.
            Eventually my curiosity got out of hand, and I started building
            Threa.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       01 · THE ORIGIN. Three strands of curiosity and frustration in
       open columns, no cards. Mono gold labels carry the structure.
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="frame warm">
    <div class="memo-shell">
      <div class="section-meta">
        <span>Why I built it</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Three problems kept coming up.</h2>

      <div class="about-duo">
        <div class="about-q">
          <span class="about-qnum">Conversation history</span>
          <h3>Lost context</h3>
          <p>
            Years of decisions and their reasoning pile up in workplace chat,
            and I rarely find them again. My memory runs on gist: I'll remember
            that we discussed something, sometimes why, rarely the exact wording
            or where we said it, though I'll know it was Kate who said it. I
            wanted to know whether I could ask Ariadne for a past decision and
            get the source conversation with it, and whether doing that well was
            affordable. I assumed it would cost too much. So far it hasn't.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-q">
          <span class="about-qnum">On your own terms</span>
          <h3>Use your own agent</h3>
          <p>
            I don't want Threa to be hard to leave, and I rarely want another
            built-in agent. Ariadne is useful inside a room because she has its
            shared context. For my own work, I want the agent I already use to
            have that context too, so Threa exposes workspace messages and memos
            through a public API, CLI, and MCP server.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-q">
          <span class="about-qnum">The chat part too</span>
          <h3>Better chat basics</h3>
          <p>
            Nested threads, quoting, replies to a specific message in a busy
            room, and formatting that behaves. These details add up over a day
            spent in chat, and I wanted them done well.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       MEET THE TEAM. Short, playful, first-person. It's one person.
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="frame">
    <div class="memo-shell is-centerpiece">
      <div class="section-meta">
        <span>Meet the team</span>
      </div>
      <h2>I'm the team.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Hi, I'm Kristoffer. People have paid me to build software for over ten
        years now. During parental leave I started tinkering on Threa to keep
        myself from going insane, and I'm not sure it worked. Here I am, up late
        after my wife has gone to bed, talking to an agent about who I am and why
        I'm building this.
      </p>
      <div class="about-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/kristofferremback" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kristofferremback/" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       HOW IT'S BUILT. Left-aligned process notes: the tools
       philosophy, then building with agents. Public repo CTAs.
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="frame warm">
    <div class="memo-shell">
      <div class="section-meta">
        <span>How it's built</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Built the way I want tools to work.</h2>
      <p class="lede about-built-lede">
        I want Threa to do its job well, work with the rest of your tools, and
        remain easy to leave. Its source and APIs stay open so you can inspect,
        change, or replace it.
      </p>
      <p class="lede about-built-lede">
        Threa has also been my way into building with AI agents. Most of it is
        written by directing them, but the thinking stays mine. They're useful
        for chasing a curiosity and still need close review. Learning where they
        help and where they fall short has been half the fun. The repo is public
        if you want to see the work in progress.
      </p>
      <div class="about-cta-row">
        <a class="os-cta" href="https://github.com/threahq/threa">Browse the source <span class="arr">→</span></a>
        <a class="os-cta" href="/developers/feature-requests">Request a feature <span class="arr">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       CLOSE
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="frame">
    <div class="memo-shell is-centerpiece about-close">
      <h2>Threa is <span class="accent">early</span> and open source.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        There's plenty left to build. Join the waitlist or follow the work in the
        public repository.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="cta" href="/#waitlist">Join the waitlist</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="brand" style="gap:10px;">
      <svg style="width:18px;height:18px;color:hsl(var(--gold));"><use href="#threa-mark" /></svg>
      <span class="wordmark" style="font-size:11px;">Threa</span>
      <span style="color:hsl(var(--muted));text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:12px;margin-left:6px;">· 2026</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ln">
      <a href="/">Product</a>
      <a href="/developers">Developer</a>
      <a href="/about">About</a>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <style>
    /* Two-column masthead: headline and framing sit side by side. */
    .about-hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
      gap: 56px;
      align-items: end;
    }
    .about-hero .lede { max-width: 460px; font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 6px; }

    /* The strands: open columns, no card chrome. A hairline rule and a mono
       label give structure without boxing them in. */
    .about-duo {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 40px;
      margin-top: 24px;
    }
    .about-q { border-top: 1px solid hsl(var(--line)); padding-top: 20px; }
    .about-qnum {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 10.5px;
      letter-spacing: 0.2em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: hsl(var(--gold));
    }
    .about-q h3 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-family: var(--font-display);
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 19px;
      line-height: 1.3;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: hsl(var(--ink));
    }
    .about-q p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: hsl(var(--ink-soft));
    }

    /* Centered profile links under the bio. Quiet mono, gold underline. */
    .about-links {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 24px;
      margin-top: 26px;
    }
    .about-links a {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: hsl(var(--gold-dim));
      text-decoration: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid hsl(var(--gold) / 0.35);
      padding-bottom: 2px;
    }
    .about-links a:hover { border-bottom-color: hsl(var(--gold)); color: hsl(var(--ink)); }

    /* Section 03 reads as personal process notes: left-aligned prose with a
       readable measure, and its "get involved" links sit under it. */
    .about-built-lede { max-width: 640px; font-size: 17px; }
    .about-built-lede + .about-built-lede { margin-top: 16px; }
    .about-cta-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 14px 28px;
      margin-top: 24px;
    }
    .about-cta-row .os-cta { margin-top: 0; }
    .about-close .actions {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 12px 18px;
      margin-top: 8px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 880px) {
      .about-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; align-items: start; }
      .about-duo { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
